; game.xon -- the kettle set: the valley above the Delve, a world of
; screens, and no descent.
;
; What this set turns on: a world of screens, (world screens W H),
; joined at their edges and kept, with the door into Kettle, the town,
; on the hub screen in the middle; open ground, (level-style open),
; with (clumps LO HI) thickets over (clump-size LO HI) square metres;
; sight to eight; hunger as a store; the rings out from the town as
; bands, each laying its caches.
; A screen's depth is its distance from the hub, so what lives on it,
; and the gold on it, grow with the walk out.  The goal is in someone's
; keeping, at the end of a chain of trades drawn each game from
; scenes.xon, and bringing it back to Kettle's square is the win.

(set "kettle")
(title "Kettle")

(world screens 7 5)

; The town is the set beside this one, a region of the same world: its
; door is on the hub (see interiors.xon), and the game starts through
; it, on the square, (start NAME) naming the door.  The Delve lies under
; the town, gone into from its pithead.
(join "town")
(start "Kettle")

; The goal: its name and its glyph; with no level it lies nowhere, and
; is given by the last link of the chain (see scenes.xon).  (chain LO
; HI) is how many links a chain has at most.
(goal "the Guild ledger" "*")
(chain 2 3)

; What a game is worth: the gold, each errand run, each screen walked
; and each door gone through, and the ledger brought home.
(score (gold 1) (quests 100) (screens 10) (places 25) (won 1000))

(player 14 16)
(unarmed 1 3)

; Food at the start; when hunger is felt; when it weakens.  Past
; nothing, (starve N) costs a hit point every N turns.
(hunger 1200 300 150)
(starve 6)

; Sight to eight cells, through nothing solid.
(view 8)

; Open ground: thickets of wall, the outer ring always clear.
(level-style open)
(clumps 8 14)
(clump-size 16 48)

(creatures 2 5)
(items 1 2)
(gold 30 6 20)
(exp 10)
(regen 12)
(wander 80)

; Classes known without being tried.
(known potion scroll)

; The rings out from the town as bands, (band NAME TO . PROPS), the
; first from the hub, each after it from the ring after the one before
; to TO: its word on first arrival, its colour, and its caches, (cache
; CLASS LO HI), that many things of CLASS a screen, each laid with a
; keeper beside it.  Any other form a band names is in front of the
; set's on its screens, and each band carves its screens in its own
; shape, (level-style STYLE): the town's own fields round its door are
; hedged closes; the farms are hedged fields either side of the road;
; the hills gritstone edges and bog; the rim limestone scars, shakeholes
; and the well-keepers' ruins.
(band "Kettle" 0 (colour 70)
  (level-style fields))
(band "The Farms" 1 (colour 70) (level-style fields)
  (enter "The farms: hedged fields and the road, the town at your back.")
  (cache potion 1 2) (cache food 1 1) (cache weapon 0 1))
(band "The Hills" 3 (colour 64) (level-style hills)
  (enter "The hills: sheep tracks through the gorse, and the bog in the low ground.")
  (cache potion 1 2) (cache food 0 1) (cache scroll 0 1) (cache armour 0 1) (cache wand 0 1))
(band "The Far Valley" 5 (colour 94) (level-style rim)
  (enter "The far valley: the old city's stones, and the Guild's men about them.")
  (cache potion 1 2) (cache wand 0 1) (cache ring 0 1) (cache armour 0 1))
